package: OpenAssetIO
author: Contributors to the OpenRV Project
organization: Academy Software Foundation
version: 1.0
rv: 2025.1
openrv: 4.1.0
requires: ''
optional: false

modes:
  - file: openassetio_mode.py
    load: immediate
  - file: openassetio_rv.py
    location: Python

description: |
  <p>
  Loads media from asset management systems through
  <a href="https://github.com/OpenAssetIO/OpenAssetIO">OpenAssetIO</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
  Set the OPENASSETIO_DEFAULT_CONFIG environment variable to the TOML
  configuration of an OpenAssetIO manager (and OPENASSETIO_PLUGIN_PATH to
  where its plugin is installed). RV then resolves the entity references
  that manager recognizes, wherever a path is accepted: command line, drag
  and drop, file browser and session files. Without a configured manager,
  this package does nothing.
  </p>
  <p>
  File &gt; Open from Asset Manager chooses the entities to load in the
  manager's own browser when its OpenAssetIO UI delegate provides one, or
  else asks for an entity reference, starting from the manager's default
  one.
  </p>
  <p>
  The entity reference of each source is saved with the session.
  File &gt; Re-resolve Asset References resolves the references of all
  loaded sources again, for example to pick up a newer version.
  </p>
  <p>
  Image sequences are supported through templated locations using the
  {frame} variable, with the frame range when the manager provides it.
  </p>
